WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:03.969
What would happen if a series of copies of
DaVinci’s Mona Lisa were put through the

00:00:03.969 --> 00:00:05.050
Clockworks?

00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:08.270
On Rough, it became a pile of shredded paper
and some pools of ink.

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:12.580
On Coarse, it became a sheet of plastic, a
sheet of paper, and more pools of ink.

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:16.660
On 1:1, it became an equally-sized copy of
DaVinci’s Vitruvian Man.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:20.760
On Fine, it became an actual painting of the
Mona Lisa on a small canvas, with the paint

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:23.619
revealed to be of modern origin by testing.

00:00:23.619 --> 00:00:28.199
On Very Fine, it became a period-accurate
16th-century painting of the Mona Lisa with

00:00:28.199 --> 00:00:30.900
hand-ground 16th Century paints.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:33.190
It now resides in Dr. Clopine’s office.

